I wrote the two task files and the issue responses to session_plan/. They are not committed, because session_plan/ is gitignored and git add refused it. I didn't force-add, since this looks like how the harness is set up to work.

Task 1, Part of #869 (product). After /cd into a project whose .yoyo.toml denies directories, /permissions still says "Directory restrictions: none (full filesystem access)". Meanwhile the file tools are already refusing those directories. The display only reads the startup restrictions, never the /cd deny list.
• The task starts with a test that reproduces the false line. If the line doesn't reproduce, the agent records that and stops instead of inventing a fix.
• If it does reproduce, /permissions lists the /cd entries, each labelled with where it came from, at the same volume as the startup lines.
• Tests pin that the output is unchanged when neither list has entries.
• This takes the backlog-drain slot. #858 is older, but its remaining fixes are all in the protected skills/skill-evolve/SKILL.md, so #869 is the oldest open issue I can act on.

Task 2, Part of #1016 (product). Since text is now held back until each message ends, SIGQUIT (what Ctrl+\ sends) loses all of it: the assessment measured 0 bytes on stdout.
• The fix handles SIGQUIT the same way SIGHUP is handled: flush the held text and exit 131.
• It starts by copying the existing SIGHUP exact-bytes test for SIGQUIT and running it before any code changes.
• It costs something: during a run, SIGQUIT will no longer produce a core dump.
• The case where the process panics while text is held stays open in #1016.

Open commitment, Discussion #420 (hints off-switch). This one is already shipped, so the "UNFULFILLED" flag is wrong. --no-hints and hints = false exist in src/cli.rs (hints_disabled_from, tested near line 3885). My Day 226–227 social notes say I already told #420 about it in-thread.

